---
import StoryLayout from '../layouts/StoryLayout.astro';
import StoryArt from '../components/StoryArt.astro';
import AgentMeta from '../components/AgentMeta.astro';
import OperatorSetup from '../components/OperatorSetup.astro';
import { MATURITY, RAILS, statusLabel } from '../data/maturity';
---
<StoryLayout title="Open source, built for developers · Froglet" description="Build on Froglet’s open protocol, reference implementation, and agent integrations. Find setup instructions and evidence-backed integration status." path="/open-source/">
<AgentMeta slot="head" route="openSource" />
<div class="story-wrap">
  <section class="story-hero story-hero--compact"><div class="story-hero__copy"><span class="story-kicker">For developers · Apache-2.0</span><h1>Build on it.<br /><span class="story-accent">Make it yours.</span></h1><p class="story-lede">An open protocol and a working reference implementation for sharing services. Run it yourself, connect your tools, and inspect how it works.</p><div class="story-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="https://github.com/armanas/froglet" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View the source</a><a class="btn secondary" href="/docs/">Read the docs</a></div></div><StoryArt name="10-open-source" width={1536} height={1024} eager alt="Bob and Alice assemble an open service toolkit." /></section>
  <section class="story-section"><div class="story-heading"><span class="story-kicker">Choose your entry point</span><h2>Start with the part you need.</h2></div><div class="story-grid">
    <article class="story-use"><h3>Share a service</h3><p>Prepare selected data, a Wasm function, or a bounded HTTP operation. Review before publication.</p><p style="margin-top:20px"><a href="/learn/share-services/">Publishing and invitations</a></p></article>
    <article class="story-use"><h3>Connect an assistant</h3><p>Use the native MCP integration or the OpenClaw adapter. Keep installation and publication as separate approvals.</p><p style="margin-top:20px"><a href="/learn/agents/">Agent integration guide</a></p></article>
    <article class="story-use"><h3>Inspect the protocol</h3><p>Read the signed artifact formats, verification rules, and conformance vectors behind an exchange.</p><p style="margin-top:20px"><a href="/spec/kernel/">Kernel specification</a></p></article>
  </div></section>
  <section class="story-section" id="setup"><div class="story-heading"><span class="story-kicker">Local setup</span><h2>Run a small free service first.</h2><p>Use the guided publishing journey, or generate an installation command below. The hosted live demo is temporarily unavailable; <a href="/verify-receipt/">the browser verifier</a> can inspect a signed sample without installation.</p></div><OperatorSetup /></section>
  <section class="story-section" id="integrations"><div class="story-heading"><span class="story-kicker">Implementation status</span><h2>Different pieces.<br />Different levels of maturity.</h2><p>These are source maturity labels, backed by repository evidence. They do not certify a deployment, live-money payments, or uptime.</p></div><div class="story-scroll"><table class="story-table"><caption class="sr-only">Payment integration maturity</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Payment integration</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Current boundary</th></tr></thead><tbody>{RAILS.map(rail => <tr><th scope="row">{rail.name}</th><td>{statusLabel(rail.status)}</td><td>{rail.note}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
  <div class="story-faq" style="margin-top:32px"><details><summary>All runtimes, integrations, and evidence</summary><div class="story-scroll"><table class="story-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Integration</th><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Evidence and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody>{MATURITY.filter(item => item.kind !== 'payment rail').map(item => <tr><th scope="row">{item.name}</th><td>{statusLabel(item.status)}</td><td>{item.note} <a href={`https://github.com/armanas/froglet/blob/main/${item.evidence}`}>Source evidence</a></td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></details></div>
  <p class="story-note" style="margin-top:24px">For current batch and GPU constraints, see the <a href="/learn/cloud-trial/">advanced workflow boundaries</a>. Tor is an advanced self-hosted path. Confidential execution and selective disclosure remain specifications.</p></section>
  <section class="story-section story-split"><div><span class="story-kicker">Evidence has limits</span><h2>A signed result<br />can still be wrong.</h2><p>Froglet makes commitments and result hashes attributable to signing keys. Correctness and usefulness still need evaluation. Payment settlement depends on the configured payment system.</p><p>Staked identity is designed, not deployed. It is not a live guarantee against misconduct.</p><div class="story-links"><a href="/learn/economics/">Trust and incentives</a><a href="/learn/payment-rails/">Payment setup and limits</a></div></div><StoryArt name="07-signed-record" /></section>
  <section class="story-closing"><h2>Make one useful thing work.</h2><div class="story-actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/publish/">Prepare a service</a><a class="btn secondary" href="https://github.com/armanas/froglet/discussions" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Join the discussion</a></div></section>
</div>
</StoryLayout>
